cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Cryptography in Python: Ciphers, Attacks, and Safe Practices"
abstract: "Executed Jupyter notebooks on number theory, classical ciphers, block ciphers, hash functions, and public-key cryptography (RSA, Diffie-Hellman, ElGamal, Rabin, elliptic curves), together with the attacks that break their weak uses: brute force, frequency analysis, key reuse, birthday collisions, ECB pattern leakage, CBC bit flipping, and malleability. Each notebook verifies its own results."
